    "html": "<p>SSR is useful when it solves a specific rendering or delivery problem. It is not automatically the right default.</p>\n<h2 id=\"what-ssr-helps-with\">What SSR helps with</h2>\n<p>The biggest gains usually show up in perceived performance, metadata delivery, and route-level content that should be visible before client bootstrapping.</p>\n<h2 id=\"where-it-costs-more\">Where it costs more</h2>\n<p>Every runtime rendering path adds operational surface area. If a route can be prerendered instead, that is often the cheaper long-term choice.</p>"
